>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `STEP_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.STEP_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Performs one fast classical-reasoning round.

`STEP_TAC thms` first saturates all open goals with deterministic safe
steps. If no safe step applies anywhere, it acts on the first goal and
tries the instantiating cascade; it considers unsafe rules only when that
cascade has no candidate. Safe and unsafe wrappers participate in their
respective parts. One call may therefore perform several safe inferences,
solve the goal, or leave residual goals. It does not run a search and has
no numeric search bound.

The theorem list modifies the current classical rule set for this call.
The markers `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`, `SDest`, `Dest` and `Del`
add or remove rules. Every unmarked theorem is inserted as an assumption
before reasoning starts. Content-bearing generic simplifier wrappers such
as `Once th` are unwrapped and inserted; inert controls such as `Cong`,
`Excl` and `SF` are ignored.

### Failure

Fails if neither safe saturation nor the fast instantiating or unsafe
cascade makes a step. A successful call need not close the goal. Malformed
extra rules can also fail during marker processing.

### Example

On the goal `p ==> p`, one call introduces `p` and then closes by
assumption:

``` hol4
classicalLib.STEP_TAC []
```

